{
  "version": 3,
  "coordinateSystem": "normalized-grid",
  "comment": "Runtime art contract for the Pulse Court Win32/GDI viewer. The 'file' value is the master/authored path (relative to the assets directory) fed into the asset pipeline; it is not what the viewer loads. All player body sheets are cleaned by scripts/clean_sprites.py into sprites/clean/ before baking; raw sprites/animated/ body sheets are source art only. Every sheet except arena.png then goes through scripts/bake_display_sprites.py, which downscales it (uniform per-sheet scale, so columns/rows/frames stay valid) to 'displayTile' pixels per frame cell and writes it to sprites/display/<basename> -- that baked file is what AssetManager::kSheets in viewer_assets.cpp actually loads. displayTile is sized to comfortably exceed the largest on-screen draw size for that sheet's category (see scripts/bake_display_sprites.py's SIZE_NOTES) now that the court's internal render resolution is capped (kCourtInternalMaxWidth in viewer_win32.cpp), so it never needs to shrink again just because a window got maximized. Re-run both scripts whenever source art changes. Frame timing is tick-based (120 Hz) and owned by the viewer's AnimationController. Frame source rectangles are computed from the normalized sheet bounds with integer rounding; some generated source sheet dimensions are not evenly divisible by their grid count.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "file": "arena.png",
      "columns": 1,
      "rows": 1,
      "frames": 1,
      "convention": "Full-court background. Preserve aspect with centered crop/fit. Not baked to sprites/display/ -- AssetManager::draw_image_cropped caches its own runtime-sized resample keyed by (id, w, h) instead."
    },
    {
      "file": "sprites/animated/ability_icons_3x1.png",
      "columns": 3,
      "rows": 1,
